  "uuid": "9cf5f21b-6fc1-4a60-9b1a-2cc7accd475a",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "13f4c6ab-752c-fe9e-840e-2dc0fa5803be",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "9b31f2ca-adb1-200c-b963-38663a772497",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Sharing his thoughts on this big achievement and the educational journey, Talha said: \"After completing my MA in Turkish Studies, with particular focus on late Ottoman history, at Sabancı University, Turkey, I wanted to broaden my knowledge in Islamic studies and improve my language skills to accomplish my own research aims at a PhD level. Hence, I decided to pursue another MA degree in London. The MA in Muslim Cultures at the Aga Khan University's Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations (AKU-ISMC) has perfectly aligned with my academic plans and goals, and the Arabic language programme being offered has increased my motivation with its intensive and helpful courses. ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Indeed, the various courses and seminars I attended here have prepared me fully and provided me with the tools and knowledge needed to move to the next step. Also, at AKU-ISMC, I have been greatly supported by my supervisor Dr Walid Ghali as well as other faculty members. As a result of these immense efforts and support, I have been accepted to study a PhD in History at Freie Universität Berlin where I am planning to conduct a research on late Ottoman Sufism.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
